 "finding": "On both slates the median-optimal build capped at $49k outscored the full-cap Safe and Balanced builds (BUF@LAR 142.98 vs 139.78/134.42; SEA@DEN 91.22 vs 73.28/88.10). Caps of $47k and below were worse on BUF@LAR and mixed on SEA@DEN. Hindsight-optimal used $49.3k and $50.0k, but the best lineup at <= $49k was within 5.2 and 0.2 points. Two slates is too small to change the public builds, so a research-only 'val' lineup (cap $49k) is now logged pre-lock and graded each slate.",
 "decision": "Track 'val' (<= $49k) alongside Safe/Balanced/Upside; promote to a public pick only if it keeps matching or beating them over several more graded slates."
